# Sodden Verdure: "This land enters tapped unless you control two or more basic lands." Turn 5 Bot1 controls a Forest (one
# basic) and a Tropical Island (the Forest and Island types, but not basic, CR 205.4c): one basic is below the two, so its
# Sodden Verdure enters tapped - though Bot2, its opponent, controls two basic lands by then. Bot2 with a Forest and an
# Island of its own plays the same land on turn 6 and it enters untapped (positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Tropical Island
Sodden Verdure
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Island
Sodden Verdure
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Tropical Island.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Sodden Verdure.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Sodden Verdure.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Sodden Verdure.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Sodden Verdure.Tapped = false
